    "answer": "`createCrashGuard` in `apps/api/src/tools/toolCrashGuard.ts` is the function that catches a tool executor that throws. It returns a `CrashGuard`, which wraps an executor in an async function with a try/catch. If the executor throws, the guard reports the crash through `reportCrash` and returns `crashResponse(name)`. If the context has been abandoned, it rethrows instead. `registerTools` wraps every executor in this guard (FR-066), so tool authors don't write their own.",
